DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270211
SUMMARY:Ash Wednesday
DESCRIPTION:Ash Wednesday opens Lent\, the forty-day season of prayer\, fas
 ting and almsgiving that ends at sundown on Holy Thursday. It is the day C
 atholics and\, increasingly\, Protestants receive a mark of ash on the for
 ehead — ash made by burning the palms blessed on the previous year's Pal
 m Sunday. In the United States it is not a holy day of obligation\, which 
 makes the size of the crowds it draws one of the more interesting things a
 bout it.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/ash-wednesday/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/ash-wednesday/
