DESCRIPTION:Good Friday is the Friday before Easter\, the day Christians co
 mmemorate the crucifixion and death of Jesus\, and the one day in the year
  on which the Catholic Church celebrates no Mass. It is not a federal holi
 day in the United States\, although the stock exchanges close for it and e
 leven states treat it as a holiday of some kind — which makes it one of 
 the harder days on the American calendar to sum up in a sentence.\n\nhttps
