UID:passover-20330414@todaycelebrates.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20330414
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20330415
SUMMARY:Passover
DESCRIPTION:Passover begins on 15 Nisan and retells the Exodus from Egypt a
 t a ritual meal\, the seder\, held in the home rather than the synagogue. 
 Because a day in the Hebrew calendar begins at sundown\, the first seder f
 alls on the evening before the Gregorian date of the first day — a disti
 nction worth holding on to when reading any calendar\, including this one.
  It runs seven days in Israel and for most Reform Jews and eight in tradit
 ional Diaspora practice\, and it is the most widely kept Jewish observance
  in the United States: six in ten American Jews told Pew they had held or 
 attended a seder in the previous year.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holi
 day/passover/
